 sales tax**:\n   - Total cost of inventory: \\( 15x + 40 \\)\n   - Sales tax rate: 8% (which can be written as 0.08)\n   - Calculate the sales tax:\n     \\[ \\text{Sales tax} = (15x + 40) \\times 0.08 = 1.2x + 3.2 \\]\n   - Total cost including sales tax:\n     \\[ 15x + 40 + 1.2x + 3.2 = 16.2x + 43.2 \\]\n\n5. **Calculate the total cost including interest**:\n   - Total cost including sales tax: \\( 16.2x + 43.2 \\)\n   - Interest rate: 5% per year\n   - Calculate the interest:\n     \\[ \\text{Interest} = (16.2x + 43.2) \\times 0.05 = 0.81x + 2.16 \\]\n   - Total cost including interest:\n     \\[ 16.2x + 43.2 + 0.81x + 2.16 = 17.01x + 45.36 \\]\n\n6. **Apply the fixed percentage discount**:\n   - Fixed percentage discount: 10%\n   - Calculate the discount:\n     \\[ \\text{Discount} = (17.01x + 45.36) \\times 0.10 = 1.701x + 4.536 \\]\n   - Total cost after discount:\n     \\[ 17.01x + 45.36 - (1.701x + 4.536) = 15.309x + 40.824 \\]\n\n7. **Set up the budget constraint**:\n   - Your budget for the total cost after applying the discount is $100.\n   - Set up the equation:\n     \\[ 15.309x + 40.824 = 100 \\]\n\n8. **Solve for the unknown variable \\( x \\)**:\n   - Subtract 40.824 from both sides:\n     \\[ 15.309x = 59.176 \\]\n   - Divide both sides by 15.309:\n     \\[ x = \\frac{59.176}{15.309} \\approx 3.88 \\]\n\n9. **Determine the total cost of the inventory and the shipping fee**:\n   - Total cost of inventory: \\( 15x + 40 \\)\n   - Substitute \\( x \\approx 3.88 \\):\n     \\[ 15 \\times 3.88 + 40 = 58.2 + 40 = 98.2 \\]\n   - Total cost including shipping fee:\n     \\[ 98.2 + 5 = 103.2 \\]\n\n10. **Calculate the total cost including interest after one year**:\n    - Total cost including interest:\n      \\[ 17.01 \\times 3.88 + 45.36 \\approx 65.96 + 45.36 = 111.32 \\]\n\n11. **Apply the fixed percentage discount**:\n    - Total cost after discount:\n      \\[ 111.32 \\times 0.90 = 99.19 \\]\n\n### Summary:\nThis example demonstrates how the order of 