umbers in cells A1 and B1:\n   - C1: `=A1+B1`\n\n4. **Check the Result**: The cell C1 should display the sum of the two numbers, which is 1241669595.\n\n5. **Verify the Sum**: To verify the sum, you can use the `SUM` function in a different cell. In cell D1, enter the formula:\n   - D1: `=SUM(A1, B1)`\n\n6. **Check the Formula**: The cell D1 should also display the sum of 1241669595.\n\nHere\u2019s what the spreadsheet might look like:\n\n```\nA    B    C    D\n564541518 677127977 1241669595 1241669595\n```\n\nBy following these steps, you can easily verify the addition of the numbers. If you find any discrepancies, you can identify and correct the error.\n\nIf you have any specific questions about the spreadsheet or need further assistance, feel free to ask! <|User|>Thank you for the detailed example using a spreadsheet. This is very helpful. Could you also show me how to use a calculator to verify the addition?\n<\uff5cAssistant\uff5c>Of course! Using a calculator is another effective way to verify the addition of large numbers. Here\u2019s how you can do it step-by-step:\n\n1. **Open a Calculator**: You can use a basic calculator on your computer, a scientific calculator, or even a calculator app on your smartphone.\n\n2. **Enter the First Number**: Start by entering the first number, which is 564541518.\n\n3. **Add the Second Number**: Press the addition (+) button and then enter the second number, which is 677127977.\n\n4. **Calculate the Sum**: Press the equals (=) button to get the result.\n\nHere\u2019s what the calculation would look like on a calculator:\n\n```\n564541518 + 677127977 = 1241669595\n```\n\nThe calculator should display the sum, which is 1241669595.\n\nIf you have any specific questions about using a calculator or need further assistance, feel free to ask! <|User|>Thank you for the detailed examples using a spreadsheet and a calculator. This has been very helpful. Could you also provide an example of using the estimation method to verify the 